===============================================
  SPECTRA FACEVOICE DASHBOARD - STARTUP GUIDE
===============================================

PROJECT OVERVIEW
----------------
This is a Next.js 16 frontend dashboard application called "SpectraFaceVoice" 
built with React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, and various UI libraries.

TECHNOLOGY STACK
----------------
- Framework: Next.js 16.2.11
- Language: TypeScript 5.x
- UI Library: React 19.2.4
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4 with PostCSS
- State Management: Zustand 5.x
- Charts: Recharts 2.x
- Animations: Framer Motion 11.x
- Icons: Lucide React
- UI Components: Radix UI primitives
- Utilities: date-fns, class-variance-authority, clsx, tailwind-merge

PREREQUISITES
-------------
1. Node.js 18.17 or later (recommended: LTS version)
2. npm (comes with Node.js) or yarn/pnpm
3. Git

SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
------------------

Step 1: Clone/Access the Project
   Navigate to the project directory:
   > cd F:\facevoicedashboard

Step 2: Install Dependencies
   Run the following command to install all required packages:
   > npm install
   
   This will install all dependencies listed in package.json including:
   - Core: next, react, react-dom
   - UI: radix-ui components, lucide-react, framer-motion
   - Charts: recharts
   - State: zustand
   - Styling: tailwindcss, postcss, tailwind-merge, clsx, class-variance-authority

   Note: node_modules/ is already present in the directory. If not, 
   run 'npm install' as shown above.

Step 3: Environment Configuration (if needed)
   This project uses .env files (gitignored). Create a .env.local file 
   in the root directory if any environment variables are required:
   > echo # Add your env variables here > .env.local

Step 4: Run the Development Server
   Start the Next.js development server:
   > npm run dev
   
   The application will be available at:
   http://localhost:3000

Step 5: Build for Production (optional)
   To create a production build:
   > npm run build
   
   Then start the production server:
   > npm start

AVAILABLE SCRIPTS
-----------------
  npm run dev       - Start development server (with hot reload)
  npm run build     - Create production build
  npm run start     - Start production server
  npm run lint      - Run ESLint for code quality checks
  npm run typecheck - Run TypeScript compiler (tsc --noEmit) for type checking

PROJECT STRUCTURE
-----------------
  src/
  ├── app/          # Next.js App Router pages and layouts
  ├── components/   # Reusable UI components
  ├── data/         # Static data and mock data
  ├── hooks/        # Custom React hooks
  ├── lib/          # Utility functions and helpers
  ├── store/        # Zustand state management stores
  └── types/        # TypeScript type definitions
  
  public/           # Static assets (images, icons, etc.)
  
  Configuration Files:
  ├── next.config.ts        # Next.js configuration
  ├── tsconfig.json         # TypeScript configuration
  ├── postcss.config.mjs    # PostCSS configuration (for Tailwind)
  ├── eslint.config.mjs     # ESLint configuration
  └── tailwind.config.*     # Tailwind CSS configuration (if present)

TROUBLESHOOTING
---------------
1. If 'npm install' fails:
   - Delete node_modules/ and package-lock.json, then run 'npm install' again
   - Ensure Node.js version is 18.17 or later: check with 'node --version'

2. If the dev server won't start:
   - Ensure port 3000 is not already in use
   - Try: npm run dev -- -p 3001 (uses port 3001 instead)

3. If you encounter TypeScript errors:
   - Run: npm run typecheck
   - Fix the reported issues

4. If you encounter ESLint errors:
   - Run: npm run lint
   - Auto-fix with: npm run lint -- --fix

5. Clearing cache:
   - Remove .next/ directory: Remove-Item -Recurse -Force .next
   - Then run 'npm run dev' again

